Logical checks

- Same person several times in the same movie (section 4):
	it happens in 951 movies, for 1,156 people.
	1,152 play DIFFERENT characters: this is normal (an actor with several roles), but be careful:
	if the movies of an actor are counted by counting the cast rows, these movies are counted twice.
	-> count the distinct (movie, actor) pairs.
	4 people appear twice with the same character, and the script shows that the character is empty:
	they are real duplicates.

- cast_id repeated in the same movie: 12 movies.

- order field (section 4):
	we expect 0, 1, 2, ... without repetitions, but:
	- in 87 movies two actors have the same order (e.g. movie 25: Jake Gyllenhaal and Scott MacDonald both 1)
	- in 6,314 movies the first value is NOT 0 (in 6,033 movies it starts from 1)
	- in 5,948 movies some numbers are missing (e.g. 0, 1, 3)
	-> to find the "first actor" of a movie you cannot look for order = 0: in 6,314 movies it does not exist.
	   The actor with the lowest order must be taken.

- Crew departments and roles (section 5):
	12 departments; 456 different roles (job).
	8 roles appear in more than one department (e.g. 'Art Direction' in Art and in Crew; 'Other' in 10 departments).
	The 'Actors' department contains 19 people (Actor 9, Stunt Double 8, Voice 2): actors that ended up in the crew.
	The 'Director' role is always in the Directing department: to find directors, job = 'Director' is enough.
	No person has the same role twice in the same movie.

- Directors (section 5):
	887 movies without a Director: 771 because the crew is empty, 116 have a crew but no director.
	91.0% of the movies have a single director, 6.0% two, 1.1% three or more.

- People with several names (section 6):
	15 people (same id) appear with two different names: it is the same name written in another
	alphabet (e.g. 'Morris Chestnut' / 'Моррис Честнат', 'Jason Momoa' / '杰森·莫玛').
	-> queries on people must be done on the id, not on the name.

- People with several genders (section 6):
	12 people have a different gender in different movies, but always "0 in some movies and 1 (or 2) in others":
	no person is both female and male. So it is not a contradiction,
	the value was simply entered in some movies and not in others.
	-> for each person the specified gender can be used when present.

- Namesakes (section 6):
	8,347 names are used by several different people (e.g. 'Michael Davis' 11 different ids).
	They may really be different people: another reason to work on the id and not on the name.

- credit_id: none repeated, it really is a unique code.

- Link with movies_metadata (section 7):
	3 movies of credits are not among the valid movies of movies_metadata: they are Midnight Man (82663),
	Mardock Scramble (122662) and Avalanche Sharks (249260), the 3 movies with the broken row.
	1 movie of movies_metadata has no credits: School's out (401840), 0 votes.
	Exactly the same situation as keywords.csv.


What emerges (section 8)
- On average 12.4 actors per movie (median 10, maximum 313) and 10.2 crew members (median 6, maximum 435).
- Actors in the most movies: Bess Flowers (240), Christopher Lee (148), John Wayne (125),
  Samuel L. Jackson (123), Michael Caine and Gérard Depardieu (110).
- Directors with the most movies: John Ford (68), Michael Curtiz (65), Werner Herzog (55), Alfred Hitchcock (53).
- In the cast men are 40.3%, women 19.9% (the rest not specified);
  in the crew men 34.6%, women 6.7%.
